1
00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:04.049
[S01] I already have a career outside of this. I don't have to be here. Why am I doing this?

2
00:00:04.440 --> 00:00:11.250
[S01] And I, I thought, you know, if I have a bad day tomorrow, I'm just, that's it. Like, I'm just done. I don't need to be here.

3
00:00:11.640 --> 00:00:17.730
[S01] And so that night I was getting ready to get into bed. I got a phone call at 11 o'clock at night.

4
00:00:17.969 --> 00:00:22.109
[S01] And it was the front desk and we were just staying in this little Italian village.

5
00:00:22.379 --> 00:00:27.269
[S01] And just this little like house in this Italian village up in the Dolomites.

6
00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:33.329
[S01] And, and so I get this phone call and they say that there's somebody downstairs to, to talk to me.

7
00:00:33.329 --> 00:00:36.810
[S01] And I was thinking, who would it be? It must be my coach, I guess.

8
00:00:37.079 --> 00:00:43.950
[S01] And so I put my pajamas on, I went downstairs and there was this young girl standing there in two prosthetic legs.

9
00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.920
[S01] With five people around her.

10
00:00:47.369 --> 00:00:52.439
[S01] And they saw on Instagram that I was in this little village.

11
00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:58.200
[S01] And they jumped in the car. They drove four hours to find me.

12
00:00:58.469 --> 00:01:03.119
[S01] They knocked down every door in that village to find me.

13
00:01:03.210 --> 00:01:03.719
[S02] Wow.

14
00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:08.519
[S01] And it was all to figure out how I snowboarded in two prosthetic legs so that she could do it too.

15
00:01:08.519 --> 00:01:11.969
[S02] That's pretty cool. Just that alone might have been worth the whole experience, right?

16
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:17.939
[S01] Well, it did. It completely changed my whole view on why I did what I did.

17
00:01:18.299 --> 00:01:26.129
[S01] And, and it took the kind of pressure of like, oh, like, you know, I'm here to win medals away completely.

18
00:01:26.310 --> 00:01:33.299
[S01] I thought that's not what it's about at all. I ended up sitting down with her. It was her grandparents and a translator and her leg maker.

19
00:01:33.299 --> 00:01:38.040
[S01] And they, you know, were all trying to figure out how I set my legs up. I spent the next hour with them.

20
00:01:38.459 --> 00:01:44.730
[S01] And when I walked away, I thought to myself immediately, I thought, that's why, that's why I do this.

21
00:01:44.939 --> 00:01:51.000
[S01] Not to win medals, not to be the best in the world, but to show other people that they can do this too.

22
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.780
[S01] Like they can live their dreams too, no matter what challenges they're faced with.

23
00:01:55.409 --> 00:02:00.060
[S01] And that changed the way I approached my training from that point forward.

24
00:02:00.359 --> 00:02:05.670
[S01] I, I knew my why so strong that it didn't matter how hard things got.

25
00:02:05.879 --> 00:02:11.719
[S01] I knew exactly why I was showing up every single day. I never asked again, why am I doing this?

26
00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:17.909
[S01] I knew why I did it. And, and it was so much more fulfilling to know that answer.

27
00:02:19.110 --> 00:02:25.860
[S01] And to not be doing it for myself, really to be doing it to show what the possibilities are so that others can,

28
00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.610
[S01] you know, but believe that they can achieve their goals as well.

29
00:02:30.150 --> 00:02:34.710
[S01] And, and to be an example of what's possible.

30
00:02:34.939 --> 00:02:41.280
[S01] And that, that just changed my whole perspective on how I,

31
00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:50.069
[S01] and approach on how I went into that Paralympic Games. I was so calm, present, appreciative.

32
00:02:50.219 --> 00:02:55.860
[S01] I brought my whole family with me to competitions, which I didn't do going into the first Paralympics that I was in.

33
00:02:56.250 --> 00:02:58.860
[S01] I was so focused in my first Paralympics that I was just like,

34
00:02:58.860 --> 00:02:59.340
[S02] They'll distract me.

35
00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:03.810
[S01] Exactly. It was like, everybody fall aside and I just focused on what I needed to do.

36
00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:08.460
[S01] But for this Paralympics, I brought my family with me. I enjoyed the ride. I enjoyed every moment.

37
00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:12.780
[S01] Even when I competed, I competed, I could have competed stronger and better, of course.

38
00:03:12.780 --> 00:03:17.969
[S01] But what I am so proud of myself of is that I was so present while I was competing.

39
00:03:18.360 --> 00:03:23.759
[S01] And, and so, yeah, I mean, there's a few different things in there.

40
00:03:23.759 --> 00:03:30.960
[S01] It's, it's knowing why you're doing what you're doing and that it's, it can't be the outcome and it can't be.
